  CTX-0001 [project] MAY_BE_STALE (docs/architecture.md changed) — YallaFlow is an AI-agnostic engineering governance layer for coding agents (Claude Code, Codex): it gives the agent durable project memory, an adaptive workflow per request, and evidence that work is actually done, so the developer describes intent instead of repeating project context in every prompt.
  CTX-0003 [project] MAY_BE_STALE (docs/architecture.md, src/agent/contract.js changed) — Core product principles: discover before asking; understand before changing; prove before claiming; remember after finishing; revalidate before trusting stale knowledge. Work history is immutable while project memory evolves. Durable state beats conversational memory. Investigation is read-only.
  CTX-0006 [tech-stack] MAY_BE_STALE (src/cli.js changed) — A Node.js (>= 20.16.0) ES-module CLI written in plain JavaScript with no build step and no TypeScript. The bin entry is src/cli.js and argument parsing uses node:util parseArgs.
  CTX-0008 [tech-stack] MAY_BE_STALE (src/cli.js changed) — There is no frontend. YallaFlow is a terminal CLI plus Markdown/YAML files it maintains inside the target repository.
