  CTX-0051 [architecture] MAY_BE_STALE (test/ticket-intake.test.js changed) — Pre-baseline engineering gate (v0.3.10-internal.4): while a project recorded as Brownfield has no approved understanding (required, in progress, or awaiting review), assertEngineeringWorkAllowed refuses creating or routing normal engineering work before any write. - Covered: start "<request>", feature/bug/investigate/change/refactor/release, intake <file>, route, and decomposition. Each fails with PROJECT_UNDERSTANDING_REQUIRED and names baseline start --objective with the shell-quoted request, or the current baseline step. - Pre-existing work stays under projectUnderstandingGate, which blocks application-writing stages and reopen. - Read-only orientation, the baseline lifecycle, and intake add stay available. Greenfield and approved Brownfield projects are never gated.
  CTX-0060 [convention] MAY_BE_STALE (CHANGELOG.md changed) — Release process (from 1.0.0): - The package follows SemVer; each release is one commit with an annotated tag vX.Y.Z matching package.json and src/version.js; tags are never moved. - Before release: npm ci + npm run check, doctor on the self-dogfood workspace, npm audit with every finding classified, npm pack --dry-run plus inspection and secret scan of the real tarball, a packed-candidate smoke test from an isolated prefix, provider/network scan, git diff --check. - CHANGELOG.md and docs/upgrading-to-*.md are updated per release; GitHub release notes live in .github/release-notes/. - Publishing: GitHub Release -> release.yml -> npm Trusted Publishing with provenance; the trusted publisher is created when the first automated release is ready because npm expires an unused configuration after 2 days. - package.json files ships src, resources, docs, README.md, CHANGELOG.md and LICENSE. - Nothing is committed, tagged, pushed or published without the maintainer's explicit approval.
  CTX-0063 [business-rule] MAY_BE_STALE (src/agent/contract.js changed) — Work routing before editing (Agent Contract v9): every intentional edit to an engineering artifact (any tracked project file other than YallaFlow state, including docs, temporary debug edits and command-generated changes) happens inside a routed work item whose guidance authorizes modification. A covering active item is reused, never duplicated. Small changes route as bounded work: in adaptive mode there is no spec or plan review, and mode-enabled gates stay human decisions. Operational help creates no work item. Tracking is never offered as optional. Untracked edits are recovered (kept, disclosed, routed with a ruling, verified fresh, never backdated). The rule is guidance only: no CLI gate or hook stops a direct write.
