  CTX-0080 [architecture] MAY_BE_STALE (src/quality/report.js changed) — Optional Smart Demo (v1.1.0, src/quality/demo.js) is independent of QC: on explicit request the Agent proposes prioritized user-facing scenarios (demo propose: audience business|developer, priority, criteria, rationale, steps, record flag, excluded items), the developer's explicit approval is recorded with their words and bound to that exact proposal's SHA-256 (demo approve --note [--only]), and demo record is refused for an unapproved or changed proposal or scenarios outside the approved scope. Approved scenarios may be split across several recordings (one video per feature or audience); coverage of the approved scope is computed across all runs of the approved proposal (approvedCoverage), never per video. Video is optional (Playwright video-start/chapter/stop; needs Playwright's ffmpeg) and stored hashed under work/<id>/quality/media/; every run carries a fixed 'not test evidence' disclaimer, and convergence refuses demo: citations. Demo and QC share the local artifact store and the report.md/report.html generator.
